.TH SKOGAI-CONFIG-GET 1  "skogai-config-get 0.0.0" 
.SH NAME
skogai\-config\-get \- print the resolved value of a key; a list prints one item per line
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskogai config get\fR [OPTIONS] <KEY>
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-origin\fR
.br
also print which layer the value came from
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR=[\fIFILE\fR]...
.br
a markdown file whose frontmatter is a layer, with its .local.md after it
.TP
\fB\-\-scope\fR=\fISCOPE\fR
.br
mount \-\-file keys under this section
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.br
Print help
.TP
<\fIKEY\fR>

.SH "ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES:"
.TP
\fISKOGAI_SYSTEM_DIR\fR [default: /etc/skogai]
.br
dir of the system layer config
.TP
\fISKOGAI_CONFIG_DIR\fR
.br
dir of the global layer, default ~/.config/skogai
.TP
\fISKOGAI_LOCAL_DIR\fR [default: .skogai]
.br
dir of the local layer; relative is from the git root, or pwd
.TP
\fISKOGAI_MODULE_PATH\fR
.br
colon\-separated dirs of module sources, default the one this module sits in
